摘要中的主要功能必须被所选片段支持。优先把改变用途含义的条件写进摘要，不能只藏在limitations。遇到“阶段1骨架”“cloud provider待实现”“匿名thread后续实现”等，摘要明确当前仅本地草稿/审批落盘，不说已实现匿名网络或云端发布。Codex/模型登录适配归coding-development；Oopz等语音房的对话连接归communication-integrations。自述兼容或性能用“作者称/README注明”，不冒充本次验证。
格式示例（仅结构，不是来源事实）：evidence:[{"paragraph_id":"p3s1","fact":"该片段支持的中文转述"}]。请从本次真实输入挑选编号。","role":"system"},{"content":"{"metadata":{"description":"A SearXNG-backed WebSearchProvider for the DeepSeek Harness web capability seam (ctx.web).","id":"gh:1334385835","install_available":true,"language":"TypeScript","name":"dsh-web-search-searxng","slug":"chinng-inta/dsh-web-search-searxng","topics":["dsh-plugin","searxng"]},"paragraphs":[{"id":"p1s1","text":"A SearXNG-backed WebSearchProvider for the DeepSeek Harness web capability seam (ctx.web)."},{"id":"p2s1","text":"# dsh-web-search-searxng"},{"id":"p3s1","text":"A SearXNG-backed `WebSearchProvider` for the\nDeepSeek Harness web capability seam (`ctx.web`)."},{"id":"p4s1","text":"SearXNG is a self-hosted metasearch engine. One search here is a plain retrieval call against the\nin"},{"id":"p4s2","text":"stance's `/search?format=json` endpoint, so unlike the shipped DeepSeek provider it needs **no API\nk"},{"id":"p4s3","text":"ey** and costs **no model turn** — the shipped provider issues a full Messages request with the\nnati"},{"id":"p4s4","text":"ve `web_search` server tool, paying latency and generated tokens for every search."},{"id":"p5s1","text":"This is an **implementation** package: it registers a provider into `ctx.web` and does **not**\nregis"},{"id":"p5s2","text":"ter a model-facing tool. `@deepseek-ai/dsh-tool-web` owns `web_search`, its schema, its prompt\nguida"},{"id":"p5s3","text":"nce, and the result card. Installing this package makes that existing tool work against your\nown ins"},{"id":"p5s4","text":"nd the result card. Installing this package makes that existing tool work against your\nown instance."},{"id":"p6s1","text":"## Install"},{"id":"p7s1","text":"### From npm"},{"id":"p8s1","text":"[代码示例省略，未执行]"},{"id":"p9s1","text":"### From this repository"},{"id":"p10s1","text":"[代码示例省略，未执行]"},{"id":"p11s1","text":"A git dependency ships no `lib/`, so the package builds itself through its `prepare` script — and\npn"},{"id":"p11s2","text":"pm blocks install scripts until you allow them. The first run therefore fails and prints the exact\nk"},{"id":"p11s3","text":"ey to allow. Add it to your profile's `pnpm-workspace.yaml` and re-run:"},{"id":"p12s1","text":"[代码示例省略，未执行]"},{"id":"p13s1","text":"The key pins a commit, so it changes whenever you install a newer revision. Building from source als"},{"id":"p13s2","text":"o\nneeds the dev toolchain fetched (~20 s versus ~2 s for the registry). Prefer npm unless you are\ntr"},{"id":"p13s3","text":"acking unreleased changes."},{"id":"p14s1","text":"### Either way"},{"id":"p15s1","text":"The package declares `dsh.bundle`, so a single command also activates it: the bundle patch\ninserts t"},{"id":"p15s2","text":"he provider row and selects it on the `web` row. Point it at your instance and restart:"},{"id":"p16s1","text":"[代码示例省略，未执行]"},{"id":"p17s1","text":"Verify the composition before booting:"},{"id":"p18s1","text":"[代码示例省略，未执行]"},{"id":"p19s1","text":"### Your instance must serve JSON"},{"id":"p20s1","text":"SearXNG does not enable the JSON API by default. In the instance's `settings.yml`:"},{"id":"p21s1","text":"[代码示例省略，未执行]"},{"id":"p22s1","text":"Without it the endpoint answers with the HTML result page, and this provider fails with a message\nna"},{"id":"p22s2","text":"ming the fix rather than a parse error."},{"id":"p23s1","text":"A public instance is a poor backend: most refuse programmatic access (HTTP 403 from a bot filter)\nor"},{"id":"p23s2","text":" rate-limit aggressively. Run your own."},{"id":"p24s1","text":"## Configuration"},{"id":"p25s1","text":"The configuration is this plugin row's `config`. `baseURL` additionally falls back to `$SEARXNG_URL`"},{"id":"p25s2","text":"\nwhen the row does not set it, so nothing else is needed to get started: export the variable and the"},{"id":"p25s3","text":"\nprovider is configured."},{"id":"p26s1","text":"Every key is declared `volatile`, which since dsh 0.1.7-rc.2 means two things: the harness settings\n"},{"id":"p26s2","text":"service may edit it, and an edit updates the running plugin **in place** (no restart). The provider\n"},{"id":"p26s3","text":"reads the row per search, so an edit reaches the next search, and clearing `baseURL` falls back to t"},{"id":"p26s4","text":"he\nenvironment again rather than stranding the provider on a value it can no longer see. Registratio"},{"id":"p26s5","text":"n\nitself never moves, so provider selection does not flicker when configuration changes."},{"id":"p27s1","text":"There are two ways to set it:"},{"id":"p28s1","text":"- **The Plugins page.** Open this package, then the configure control on its `web-search-searxng`\n[该"},{"id":"p28s2","text":"e Plugins page.** Open this package, then the configure control on its `web-search-searxng`\n[该节后续省略]"},{"id":"p29s1","text":"## Known limitations"},{"id":"p30s1","text":"- **`maxResults` is not pushed down.** SearXNG exposes no result-count parameter, so the instance\nre"},{"id":"p30s2","text":"turns its full first page and the seam truncates. This bounds tokens, not the instance's work.\n- **`"},{"id":"p30s3","text":"publishedDate` is usually absent.** General web engines rarely date results; news engines\nusually do"},{"id":"p30s4","text":". Filter with `categories: ['news']` if you need dates.\n- **Infoboxes are not surfaced.** They are s"},{"id":"p30s5","text":"tructured entity cards rather than an answer to the\nquery, so flattening them into `content` would p"},{"id":"p30s6","text":"resent them as one.\n- **No per-engine failure reporting.** SearXNG reports `unresponsive_engines[]` "},{"id":"p30s7","text":"on partial failures;\nthe seam's result shape has nowhere to put it, so a degraded search looks like "},{"id":"p30s8","text":"failures;\nthe seam's result shape has nowhere to put it, so a degraded search looks like a thin one."},{"id":"p31s1","text":"## Compatibility"},{"id":"p32s1","text":"| This package | DeepSeek Harness |"},{"id":"p33s1","text":"| `0.5.0`+ | `0.1.7-rc.2` |\n| `0.4.0` | `0.1.2-rc.1` – `0.1.5-rc.3` |\n| `0.3.3` – `0.3.x` | `0.1.0-r"},{"id":"p33s2","text":"c.8` – `0.1.1-rc.2` |\n| `0.1.x` – `0.3.2` | `0.1.0-rc.6` |"},{"id":"p34s1","text":"**Every row is mutually exclusive**: nothing here is backward compatible, and nothing older is\nforwa"},{"id":"p34s2","text":"rd compatible. Installing the wrong pair does not merely lose this card — it fails the whole\nWeb UI'"},{"id":"p34s3","text":"s plugin load, because the breakages surface as an unanswerable client `require` or an\ninvalid slot "},{"id":"p34s4","text":"ause the breakages surface as an unanswerable client `require` or an\ninvalid slot registration (#1):"},{"id":"p35s1","text":"- rc.8 dropped `@deepseek-ai/dsh-client-web-react` from the loader's seed table. Up to `0.3.2`\nthis "},{"id":"p35s2","text":"package imported `bindSnapshotSelector` from it. `0.3.3` hands its store to the renderer\nthrough the"},{"id":"p35s3","text":" slot inject face's `hooks` compartment instead, which is where rc.8 synthesizes\nselector hooks.\n- r"},{"id":"p35s4","text":"c.8 turned `settings.plugin.item` from a `list` slot (`id` + `order`) into a `keyed` one\n(`key` = th"},{"id":"p35s5","text":"e settings namespace the card edits). `0.3.3` registers the keyed way, which rc.6\nrejects.\n- 0.1.2-a"},{"id":"p35s6","text":"lpha.1 deleted `@deepseek-ai/dsh-client-runtime` outright. Up to `0.3.x` this package\ntook `createSn"},{"id":"p35s7","text":"apshotStore` from it and named it in `dsh.client.inject`; `0.4.0` takes the same\nfunction from `@dee"},{"id":"p35s8","text":"pseek-ai/dsh-client-store` (a seed the frontend now hands the loader) and\ndrops the phantom from `in"},{"id":"p35s9","text":"ject`, which would otherwise leave the row pending forever.\n- 0.1.2-alpha.2 deleted the `settingsNam"},{"id":"p35s10","text":"espace()` and `installSettingsSection()` helpers from\n`@deepseek-ai/dsh-settings`. `0.4.0` uses a ba"},{"id":"p35s11","text":"re namespace literal and calls\n`settings.installSection` inside `ctx.inject(['settings'], …)`, which"},{"id":"p35s12","text":" is now the attach/detach\nlifecycle.\n- 0.1.7-rc.2 removed the shared `settings.yaml` together with `"},{"id":"p35s13","text":"settings.installSection`: settings\nbecame each plugin row's own `config`, editable where the schema "},{"id":"p35s14","text":"marks a field `volatile` and\ndelivered to `apply` as live references. `0.5.0` marks every key volati"},{"id":"p35s15","text":"le and reads them per search;\n`0.4.0`'s host half calls the removed method, so its settings never at"},{"id":"p35s16","text":"tach. The same release deleted the settings page's\n[该节后续省略]"}],"truncated":true}","role":"user"}],"model":"MiniMax-M3.1-Flash","reasoning_effort":"low","stream":false}
